      "role": "user",
      "content": "thanks. i'm looking at the sequence now and everything seems to follow the docs perfectly. i've even tried re-sending the exact same payload in the stripe dashboard/cli and it still hits that 402. it's driving me crazy because it feels like there's some invisible error happening in the background. is there any way to perform a more granular trace to see if there is some kind of internal validation error that isn't being surfaced in the main error message?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "If the Stripe Dashboard or CLI is also returning the 402 with the same vague message, then the problem is almost certainly *outside* of your application's code, which is frustrating. It's less about your payload structure and more about the environment or the account itself. You need to dig deeper into the Stripe logs associated with that specific transaction ID, not just the API response.\n\nYou should contact Stripe Support directly, providing them with the exact timestamp and the transaction ID that is failing. They have access to the internal processing logs that are far more granular than what the public API surfaces. They can tell you if their system is rejecting the request due to a regional block, compliance issue, or some other internal validation failure.",
